  "timing_scope": {
    "name": "unproved inference, weights resident",
    "parts": {
      "prefill": "one `max_new_tokens=1` call: the whole prompt read, and the first generated position emitted",
      "decode": "the rest of the full call, by difference: the remaining generated positions, one step each",
      "end_to_end": "the full call on its own: the prompt prefilled and every generated position decoded, as one wall-clock time"
    },
    "includes": [
      "the forward passes that produce the measured positions",
      "sampling/argmax, KV-cache growth, the engine's own scheduling"
    ],
    "excludes": [
      "process start, weight load and any compile/CUDA-graph capture (the warmup passes run before the timed repetitions and make the same two calls, generating the same token count, so no timed repetition is the first full-length decode of the process)",
      "tokenization of the prompt (built once, outside the timed region)"
    ],
    "comparable_to": "the proved side's timing scopes, with one thing said out loud: none of them contains an inference pass. `whole wall` is trace generation, interaction generation, stwo and serialization; `loop`, which adds the witness read and the layer build, still reads a witness a prior extraction produced. So a proved cost per position is prover-seconds and an unproved one is inference-seconds, and a deployment that must both infer and prove pays the sum of the two."
  },
